  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Rows: 7 (Legendary) + 404 (Historical) = 323 rulers with accession dates and 88 heading rows (dynasty name/dates, 'Family name', 'Capital(s)') with Accession left \"\".",
   "Printed in two columns per page, pp. 93 (right column only) to 97 (top two lines, set in two side-by-side pairs); combined into one continuous list in reading order (p. 97: left pair then right pair).",
   "Headings printed over two lines (e.g. 'Capitals: Feng (1122-771)' / 'Loyang (770-255)'; 'The Shang or Yin Dynasty—' / '1766-1122 B.C.') are joined into one cell with a space; ruler names that wrap onto a second line likewise joined.",
   "Section labels 'LEGENDARY' and 'HISTORICAL' printed in capitals; given here as part labels in Title Case.",
   "p. 93 Shang dynasty: accession dates drift upward relative to the names near the foot of the column; 22 names and 22 dates counted and assigned in order.",
   "'Yin Ti' (Later Han, p. 96) printed 'A. D. 948' with a space; kept as printed.",
   "Two consecutive rulers under Chou both printed 'Ching Wang' (544 B.C., 519 B.C.); Ming 'Tai Tsung' A.D. 1449, Liao dynasty 'A.D. 907-1154' etc. kept as printed. Liao and Chin (Golden) dynasties print no Family name/Capital lines.",
   "No totals printed. No unreadable cells."
